        "title": "The Compiler Pipeline, Front to Back - Landscape",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "A compiler is a function from source text to machine code, but the interesting\nstructure is the *pipeline* that function factors into. The factoring is not\narbitrary: it isolates language-specific concerns (the frontend), target-specific\nconcerns (the backend), and the language-and-target-independent optimization\nmachinery in the middle. The single most consequential idea in modern compiler\nengineering — LLVM's organizing principle — is that the middle can be *shared*."
    }
